Audit-only headers for scripts/audit-libc16 (docs/M3-RUNTIME-AUDIT.md).

They stand in for what libc16's and libkitchen16's headers lack, so that
every module of the interpreter can be compiled against them and the
symbols it would then need can be listed. They are never used to build
PERL.EXE, and they are not a design for the eventual headers: each one
declares only what the Perl 3.044 sources and perl16's own files use.

audit.h is force-included (wcc -fi) and supplies the few macros that
libc16's headers lack (errno values, stdaux/stdprn), and P16_CB, the
callback convention msdos/p16rt.h gives the runtime build (#16).
varargs.h stands in for the pre-ANSI <varargs.h> that util.c uses; M3.4
moves it to <stdarg.h> (#16).

setjmp.h, signal.h, process.h and math.h stood in for headers that libc16
0.12 and libkitchen16 0.02 now provide, and were removed when perl16
pinned those releases.

Sources: ISO/IEC 9899:1990; POSIX.1-1990 for the errno names. Nothing
here was taken from Open Watcom's or any other runtime's headers.
